[Term]
id: GO:0015894
name: acriflavine transport
namespace: biological_process
def: "The directed movement of acriflavine into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. Acriflavine is a fluorescent dye used as a local antiseptic and also as a biological stain. It intercalates into nucleic acids thereby inhibiting bacterial and viral replication." [GOC:curators, PubChem_Compound:6842]
