[Term]
id: GO:0018981
name: triethanolamine metabolic process
namespace: biological_process
def: "The chemical reactions and pathways involving triethanolamine, a combustible, hygroscopic, colorless liquid commonly used in dry-cleaning solutions, cosmetics, detergents, textile processing, wool scouring, and as a corrosion inhibitor and pharmaceutical alkalizing agent." [GOC:jl]
