namespace: biological_process
def: "OBSOLETE. The increase in size or mass of symbiont, or the progression of the symbiont from an initial condition to a later condition, occurring on or near its host phyllosphere. The host phyllosphere is defined as total above-ground surfaces of a plant as a habitat for symbiont. The host is defined as the larger of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [GOC:pamgo_curators]

[Term]
id: GO:0075014
name: obsolete growth or development of symbiont on or near host rhizosphere
namespace: biological_process
