property_value: term_tracker_item "This term was obsoleted because it represents a molecular function." xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GO:0075078
name: obsolete modulation by host of symbiont receptor-mediated signal transduction
namespace: biological_process
def: "OBSOLETE. Any process in which the host organism modulates the frequency, rate or extent of receptor-mediated signal transduction in the symbiont. The receptor is defined as a protein on the cell membrane or within the cytoplasm or cell nucleus that binds to a specific molecule (a ligand) such as a neurotransmitter or a hormone or other substance, and initiates the cellular response to the ligand. The host is defined as the larger of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [GOC:pamgo_curators]

