[Term]
id: GO:0075187
name: hyphopodium formation
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process in which a specialized structure, consisted of stalked, thick-walled, lobed cells of vegetative epiphytic hyphae, is formed, to attach and penetrate the host surface. The host is defined as the larger of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [GOC:pamgo_curators]
