[Term]
id: GO:0080154
name: regulation of fertilization
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process that modulates the rate, frequency or extent of fertilization. Fertilization is the union of gametes of opposite sexes during the process of sexual reproduction to form a zygote. It involves the fusion of the gametic nuclei (karyogamy) and cytoplasm (plasmogamy)." [GOC:DHL, PMID:20478994]
is_a: GO:2000241 ! regulation of reproductive process
relationship: regulates GO:0009566 ! fertilization

[Term]
id: GO:0080155
name: regulation of double fertilization forming a zygote and endosperm
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process that modulates the rate, frequency or extent of double fertilization forming a zygote and endosperm. Double fertilization forming a zygote and endosperm is a type of fertilization where one of the two sperm nuclei from the pollen tube fuses with the egg nucleus to form a 2n zygote, and the other fuses with the two polar nuclei to form the 3n primary endosperm nucleus and then develops into the endosperm. The ploidy level of the 2n zygote and 3n primary endosperm nucleus is determined by the ploidy level of the parents involved. An example of this component is found in Arabidopsis thaliana." [GOC:DHL, PMID:20478994]
is_a: GO:0080154 ! regulation of fertilization
relationship: regulates GO:0009567 ! double fertilization forming a zygote and endosperm

