is_a: GO:0086100 ! endothelin receptor signaling pathway
is_a: GO:0086103 ! G protein-coupled receptor signaling pathway involved in heart process

[Term]
id: GO:0086102
name: adenylate cyclase-inhibiting G protein-coupled acetylcholine receptor signaling pathway involved in negative regulation of heart rate
namespace: biological_process
def: "An  adenylate cyclase-inhibiting G protein-coupled acetylcholine receptor signaling pathway  that contributes to a decrease in frequency or rate of heart contraction through inhibition of adenylate cyclase (AC) activity. Binding of acetylcholine to a G protein-coupled (muscarinic) receptor on the surface of the signal-receiving cell results in the activation of an intracellular Gi/o protein. Gi/o inhibits adenylate cyclase to decrease cyclic-AMP (cAMP) levels. Since cAMP binds directly to F-channels to allow an inward flow of sodium (funny current, If current), a reduction in cAMP reduces the funny current to bring about membrane hyperpolarization and a decrease in heart rate." [GOC:BHF, GOC:mtg_cardiac_conduct_nov11]
is_a: GO:0007197 ! adenylate cyclase-inhibiting G protein-coupled acetylcholine receptor signaling pathway
is_a: GO:0086033 ! G protein-coupled acetylcholine receptor signaling pathway involved in negative regulation of heart rate

