name: amniotic stem cell differentiation
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process whereby a relatively unspecialized cell acquires specialized features of an amniotic stem cell. An amniotic stem cell is a mesenchymal stem cell extracted from amniotic fluid. Amniotic stem cells are able to differentiate into various tissue types such as skin, cartilage, cardiac tissue, nerves, muscle, and bone." [CL:0002639, GOC:yaf, PMID:20942606, Wikipedia:Amniotic_stem_cells]
is_a: GO:0072497 ! mesenchymal stem cell differentiation

[Term]
