[Term]
id: GO:0097241
name: hematopoietic stem cell migration to bone marrow
namespace: biological_process
def: "The orderly movement of a hematopoietic stem cell into the bone marrow, and its subsequent positioning within defined functional compartments in that microenvironment. A hematopoietic stem cell is a cell from which all cells of the lymphoid and myeloid lineages develop, including blood cells and cells of the immune system." [CL:0000037, GOC:yaf, PMID:17368745]
