[Term]
id: GO:0120125
name: PNGase complex
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A protein complex responsible for the catalysis of the reaction: 4-N-(N-acetyl-D-glucosaminyl)-protein + H2O = N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminylamine + peptide L-aspartate. This reaction is the hydrolysis of an N4-(acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl)asparagine residue in which the N-acetyl-D-glucosamine residue may be further glycosylated, to yield a (substituted) N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminylamine and the peptide containing an aspartic residue." [GOC:lnp, PMID:15964983, PMID:16249333]
is_a: GO:1905368 ! peptidase complex

