[Term]
id: GO:0120148
name: host cell centrosome
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A structure in a host cell comprised of a core structure (in most organisms, a pair of centrioles) and peripheral material from which a microtubule-based structure, such as a spindle apparatus, is organized. Centrosomes occur close to the nucleus during interphase in many eukaryotic cells, though in animal cells it changes continually during the cell-division cycle." [ISBN:0198547684]
is_a: GO:0044163 ! host cytoskeleton

[Term]
id: GO:0120149
name: host cell peroxisome
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A small host cell organelle enclosed by a single membrane, and found in most eukaryotic cells. Contains peroxidases and other enzymes involved in a variety of metabolic processes including free radical detoxification, lipid catabolism and biosynthesis, and hydrogen peroxide metabolism." [PMID:9302272]
