[Term]
id: GO:1990050
name: phosphatidic acid transfer activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Removes a phosphatidic acid from a membrane or a monolayer lipid particle, transports it through the aqueous phase while protected in a hydrophobic pocket, and brings it to an acceptor membrane or lipid particle. Phosphatidic acid refers to a glycophospholipids with, in general, a saturated fatty acid bonded to carbon-1, an unsaturated fatty acid bonded to carbon-2, and a phosphate group bonded to carbon-3." [PMID:23042293]
is_a: GO:0120014 ! phospholipid transfer activity

[Term]
