is_a: GO:0019899 ! enzyme binding

[Term]
id: GO:1990227
name: paranodal junction maintenance
namespace: biological_process
def: "The maintenance of a paranodal junction, a highly specialized cell-cell junction found in vertebrates, which forms between a neuron and a glial cell, and has structural similarity to Drosophila septate junctions. A paranodal junction flanks the node of Ranvier in myelinated nerve, electrically isolates the myelinated from unmyelinated nerve segments, and physically separates the voltage-gated sodium channels at the node from the cluster of potassium channels underneath the myelin sheath." [GOC:pr, PMID:24011083]
is_a: GO:0045217 ! cell-cell junction maintenance

