is_a: GO:0097201 ! negative regulation of transcription from RNA polymerase II promoter in response to stress

[Term]
id: GO:1990442
name: intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway in response to nitrosative stress
namespace: biological_process
def: "The series of molecular signals in which an intracellular signal is conveyed to trigger the apoptotic death of a cell. The pathway is induced in response to nitrosative stress; a state often resulting from exposure to high levels of nitric oxide (NO) or the highly reactive oxidant peroxynitrite, which is produced following interaction of NO with superoxide anions." [GOC:bf, GOC:PARL, PMID:23985028]
is_a: GO:0071500 ! cellular response to nitrosative stress
is_a: GO:0097193 ! intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway

