namespace: biological_process
def: "The process by which synaptic transmission, induced by the arrival of a spike (action potential) at a synapse, acts to increase the amount of neurotransmitter released in response to the arrival of subsequent spikes.  This effect is seen when a train of closely space spikes arrives at a synapse with a low initial release probability.  It occurs in a timeframe of tens to hundreds of milliseconds." [GOC:dos, GOC:sp, ISBN:9780071120005, PMID:11826273, PMID:26738595]
is_a: GO:0048167 ! regulation of synaptic plasticity

[Term]
